    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Case DSP-02725 (trip TRP-02725), contested charge SGD 4.50. This is addressed to both of you.\n\nTHE ARRIVAL MARKER WAS FALSE. Driver, your 'I'm Here' tap at 18:15:10 did not coincide with your arrival: the trace shows the first qualifying in-geofence fix only at 18:17:10, 120 seconds later (EV-GPS-02725, derived dwell_start_offset_sec −120.0), the trace's moving speeds begin at 32.2 km/h — above the 15 km/h POL-NS-05 trigger — and you said yourself you 'pressed arrived a bit early'. Under POL-NS-05 the tap does not start the waiting clock, and the clock is recomputed from 18:17:10.\n\nTHAT CORRECTION DOES NOT DEFEAT THE FEE. From 18:17:10 to 18:20:40 you held position inside the 50 m STANDARD geofence continuously for 210 seconds on 22 qualifying fixes, against a free waiting period of 180 seconds in force for this trip (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec; the derived STANDARD minimum is the same 180 s). POL-NS-05(iii) therefore applies: the false marker is recorded as a referral but does not defeat the fee.\n\nRIDER, YOUR MAIN ARGUMENT IS REJECTED. You say the required minimum is 300 seconds (fee_schedule.minimum_dwell_sec STANDARD) and the dwell is 30 seconds short. POL-NS-01(c) and POL-NS-06 both measure the requirement by the free waiting period in force, and the fee schedule's own resolution rule says minimum_dwell_sec is retained only to interpret pre-version-2 records and is never applied to a record that carries platform_policy — this record does. On the correct 180-second requirement the 210-second dwell is 30 seconds OVER, not under; the derived figure of −30.0 seconds (shortfall_basis longest_run_sec, EV-GPS-02725) is a surplus. Your strict-liability point under POL-NS-06 therefore has nothing to operate on, and your fare claim does not produce a refund.\n\nALL FOUR LIMBS OF POL-NS-01 HOLD. (a) an 'arrived' event; (b) in-geofence position on the POL-NS-05 recomputed clock; (c) 210 s of continuous dwell against the 180 s requirement; (d) no boarding event, and the driver terminated at 18:20:41 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, after the waiting period expired at 18:20:10. No clause displaces the fee: POL-NS-02 is satisfied by the in-radius fixes; POL-NS-03 does not apply because your stationary fixes lie inside the arrival radius, not outside it; POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider — the chat log holds only the driver's single message at 18:15:30, so limb (a) fails, and the rider's own track places the device 843.6 m from the pin with zero qualifying fixes inside the 100 m radius, so limb (c) fails affirmatively. Your suggestion that the rider's stationary track contradicts the RIDER_NO_SHOW code is rejected: a device 843.6 m from the pickup point is consistent with the rider not being at the pickup point, and the only apparent conflict — the early tap against the trace — is resolved by POL-NS-05, so POL-NS-09(b) is not engaged.\n\nRESULT. The SGD 4.50 fee stands; on the fee the rider's claim is not supported and no refund issues (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00 left as they are). Under POL-NS-07 the driver is compensated at 80% of the SGD 4.50 net fee = SGD 3.60; the anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d 1, below 4, and 1/65 = 0.015, below 0.08), so compensation is paid rather than withheld. On a DRIVER_COMPENSATION ruling amount_sgd carries the same SGD 3.60 — it is the amount this ruling moves, not a second payment and not a refund to the filing party.\n\nWEIGHTS AND CONFIDENCE. The deciding facts rest on EV-GPS-02725, EV-TRIP-02725, EV-FARE-02725 and EV-DPROF-02725, all at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0; confidence is 0.95, above the 0.70 floor. EV-ADVIS-02725-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 (issue MISSING_ARTIFACT), but nothing rests on it: no accumulation across intervals is required, because the single in-geofence run already exceeds the minimum. Two claims that cited that missing advisory without naming its issue code were discarded by the referee and appear in the audit below.\n\nPROFILE FIELDS. Two rider claims mention the driver's rating (4.31) and prior_deviation_flags, and the rider's prior_no_show_flags. Those fields are context-only under POL-GEN-01, and both claims cite them expressly for no adverse finding; they carry no weight and no claim is discarded on that account.\n\nPOL-GEN-05: the monetary effect is SGD 3.60, below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so it executes automatically, subject to appeal under POL-GEN-04."
  },
